A markdown fence that says `mode=` becomes components rather than text.

The trailer sits on the info line -- ` ```sngl mode=island ` -- so goldmark's
`Language()` still reports `sngl` and a fence that writes no trailer still
highlights through the chroma path every other fence uses.

Four modes, and what separates them is which scope the source lands in.
`view` is the default and is shown and not compiled. `island` is a component
of its own, inserted where the fence was. `package` is package-level
declarations and renders nothing. `body` is the statements it holds, placed
into the document's own component body at the position written.

None of the three live modes also *shows* its source: an example is what it
does, and a document that wants both writes both.

An island's isolation is the language's own. The whole fence goes in the
component's body, so a `var` there is that component's state and a nested
declaration is scoped to that body: the two islands below each write `var n`
and neither reaches the other, which the emitted page shows as two counters
with different values.

Imports are hoisted, since a fence is spliced into a body and an import may
only be written at the root of a file. They are kept as written and collapsed
when redundant -- both islands import `sngl:ui` as `ui`, which is the same
import twice and comes out once, and once more is what the generated package
already wrote for itself. A genuine conflict is not renamed here: rewriting an
alias means resolving every name under it, which is checking, so it is left to
reach the checker as the program it is.

deny * `var n` -- an island shows nothing of its source: the two below appear only as what they render
deny * `function double` -- the package fence's func folds into the expression that called it; nothing survives under its name
deny * `island1` -- and an island is inlined like any other component, so no factory is emitted under its name

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import doc "md:./guide.md"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

ui.window #home(title="live") {
    doc.document
}
-- guide.md --
# Live

```sngl mode=package
func double(n int) int {
    return n * 2
}
```

A counter:

```sngl mode=island
import ui "sngl:ui"

var n = 1

ui.text(value="n doubled is {double(n)}")
```

Another, which does not share it:

```sngl mode=island
import ui "sngl:ui"

var n = 100

ui.text(value="n is {n}")
```

Straight into the body:

```sngl mode=body
import ui "sngl:ui"

ui.divider(label="from a body fence")
```

And an ordinary sample, shown and not compiled:

```sngl
const shown = 1
```
